S5-07 counted canonical common-ID N=2 — 2026-11-17

Result
------
The fresh `stage4-init-nonce` series completed two runs with unique generated
nonces. Both run scenarios passed: each reached the 3,000,000,000 instruction
budget (`retired=2,999,999,998`), validated its exact nonce markers, and had the
expected syscall order `[83,165,257,0,3,1,39,35,60]`. Both manifests recorded
`counted` acceptance, Stage4A, CPL0 set, user mode, RAM 128 MiB, and no
diagnostic randomization flags. The series profile is still
`smoke_not_acceptance`; counted run eligibility is not Stage 5 scenario
acceptance. The host was macOS/aarch64, release runner
0.1.0, source revision `dd7712141f582117cf0ab2c2fa28e6b44f9646d5`, clean.

The series outcome is `passed` for the two individual scenarios, but strict
within-series comparison is `matches=false` with exactly these unexplained
items:

* `run[1].machine_observations differs`
* `run[1].ordered_uart_bytes differs after nonce normalization`

Thus this is a counted common-ID N=2 experiment, not a successful S5-07
acceptance series. No comparator or eligibility rule was changed.

Eligibility / terminal panic normalization
------------------------------------------
All scalar/configuration/syscall eligibility conditions pass. Terminal panic
normalization is disabled because each panic backtrace contains optional frames
not in the current allowlist. Run 1's first rejected frame is `? psi_task_switch`
(UART line 328); additional rejected frames are `__schedule`, `schedule`,
`do_nanosleep`, `hrtimer_nanosleep`, `__pfx_hrtimer_wakeup`,
`__x64_sys_nanosleep`, and `set_ptes.isra.0`. Run 2's first rejected frame is
`? schedule` (UART line 331); its additional rejected frames are
`do_nanosleep`, `hrtimer_nanosleep`, `__pfx_hrtimer_wakeup`, and
`__x64_sys_nanosleep`.
`normalize_stage4_panic_snapshot` returns `None` for an unknown optional frame,
which also disables UART and machine volatile-observation normalization. Merely
adding these frames to the allowlist would not make this series match.

Residual machine observations
-----------------------------
After applying the existing machine-volatility removals offline, the following
strict values still differ:

| Observation | Run 1 | Run 2 |
| --- | ---: | ---: |
| `cr3_changes` | 26,617 | 26,618 |
| `exceptions_delivered` | 34 | 35 |
| `page_faults_delivered` | 33 | 34 |
| `rdtsc_reads` | 34,429,691 | 34,440,164 |
| CPL0 `rdtsc_reads_by_cpl` | 34,429,691 | 34,440,164 |

`general_protection_faults_delivered=1`, CPL3 retired instructions `=1,093`,
and halt wakes `=2` agree. The aggregate fault counts do not identify the differing
fault event: these source outputs contain no per-fault history or observation
sidecar. The optional panic frames and the extra page fault are separate
observations; no causal link is established.

